064a"], "language": "arabic", "country": ["egypt", "qatar", "saudi arabia", "morocco", "kuwait", "united arab emirates", "algeria", "bahrain", "jordan", "tunisia"], "category": ["sports"], "datatype": "news", "pubDate": "2026-08-15 15:54:49", "pubDateTZ": "UTC", "fetched_at": "2026-08-15 16:01:43", "image_url": "https://assets.kooora.com/images/v3/imago-sport-1081064019/crop/MM5DKMBQGQ5DEOBRGU5G433XMU5DAORSGYYQ====/imago-image.jpeg?auto=webp&format=jpg&quality=80", "video_url": null, "source_id": "kooora", "source_name": "\u0643\u0648\u0648\u0648\u0631\u0629", "source_priority": 4562, "source_url": "https://www.kooora.com", "source_icon": "https://n.bytvi.com/kooora.jpg", "sentiment": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN PROFESSIONAL AND CORPORATE PLANS", "sentiment_stats": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN PROFESSIONAL AND CORPORATE PLANS", "ai_tag": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN PROFESSIONAL AND CORPORATE PLANS", "ai_region": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN CORPORATE PLANS", "ai_org": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN CORPORATE PLANS", "ai_summary": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN PAID PLANS", "duplicate": false}, {"article_id": "9c948406fc6e05aaa3dc3911ecb4d508", "link": "https://saudigazette.com.sa/article/663748/world/burhan-says-sudan-army-open-to-genuine-peace-but-vows-to-defeat-rsf", "title": "Burhan says Sudan army open to \u2018genuine\u2019 peace but vows to defeat RSF", "description": "PORT SUDAN \u2014 Sudan\u2019s Sovereignty Council Chairman Abdel Fattah Al-Burhan said the army remains determined to defeat the paramilitary Rapid Support Forces (RSF), while stressing that it remains open to \u201cgenuine\u201d initiatives aimed at ending the conflict.In an address marking the 72nd anniversary of the Sudanese Armed Forces, Al-Burhan said the army\u2019s determination to fight and defeat the RSF \u201cdoes not mean turning a blind eye to any genuine initiative for peace,\u201d according to the state news agency SUNA.\u201cOur efforts toward this have not stopped since the first months of the rebellion, but we will not accept an incomplete peace or a peace that returns the criminals and killers, the Dagalo militia and its supporters, to power or participation in it,\u201d he said, referring to RSF leader Mohamed Hamdan Dagalo.Al-Burhan said the army\u2019s conditions for peace have remained clear since May 2023, beginning with the RSF laying down its weapons and gathering in designated areas.He said civilians must also be allowed to return to their homes and normal life restored, including basic services, security and protection.\u201cAfter that, the situation of fighters who are not criminals can be considered,\u201d he added.On the political track, Al-Burhan said he had begun dialogue with national and sectoral groups that supported the Sudanese state, its unity and institutions, with the aim of involving them in completing state institutions, including the legislative council.He described the establishment of the legislative council as \u201ca constitutional requirement.\u201dAl-Burhan also welcomed an independently launched initiative seeking to establish a \u201cpurely Sudanese dialogue\u201d involving political and societal forces.He said the initiative aims to establish an independent national mechanism to prepare for a comprehensive dialogue and build broad national consensus capable of putting Sudan on a path toward stability.According to Al-Burhan, those behind the initiative requested state guarantees to facilitate the participation and safety of all parties.He said he had approved the request, pledging the state\u2019s readiness to provide logistical support as well as legal, political and security guarantees for the dialogue.Sudan has been engulfed in war between the army and the RSF since April 2023. The conflict has killed tens of thousands of people and displaced nearly 13 million, according to UN and international estimates.", "content": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN PAID PLANS", "keywords": ["world"], "creator": ["agencies"], "language": "english", "country": ["saudi arabia"], "category": ["w